+# Aegis Data Platform Overview (scaffold)
+
+This patch adds scaffolding for a complete data platform. It includes:
+- Trino deployment (SQL/OLAP)
+- Kafka local compose for streaming
+- Airflow DAG example for batch ETL with Great Expectations validation
+- JDBC -> S3 connector example
+- DataHub metadata bootstrap helper
+- Feast feature store sample repo configuration and ingest script
+- MLflow quick server and example logging
+- DVC pipeline skeleton for dataset versioning
+- Audit logger for dataset access events
+- Prometheus rules for data pipeline SLAs
+
+How to get started:
+1. Provide infrastructure: S3 bucket, Redis (for Feast), Postgres/RDS (for Airflow metadata), object store credentials (AWS/GCP).
+2. Deploy Trino and connect to your Hive metastore (or use Trino catalog for S3).
+3. Run Kafka locally (docker-compose) for dev streaming; use managed Kafka for prod.
+4. Deploy DataHub (or Data Catalog of choice) and run bootstrap script to ingest dataset metadata.
+5. Initialize DVC in repo and create dataset snapshots for reproducibility.
+6. Wire MLflow to your model registry and storage.
+7. Harden RBAC, SSO, encryption, and backups for production readiness.
+
+Use the code and templates in ops/ to customize to your environment.
+
